.SH NAME
le-datacenter - Read fleet, GPU and inventory evidence from approved sources


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle datacenter [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
One-shot read-only Prometheus/DCGM and NetBox views. No discovery, agents or remote controls.
Use --demo for invented offline data. Missing data is unknown, never assumed zero.
Tokens are environment-only; use LOCALHOST_PROMETHEUS_TOKEN and LOCALHOST_NETBOX_TOKEN through Varlock.
Live URLs require HTTPS except explicit literal loopback. Requests, pagination and output are bounded.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--demo\fP[=false]
	Invented offline fixture; ignores credentials and makes no requests

.PP
\fB--details\fP[=false]
	Include NetBox device/site/rack/owner names in output

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for datacenter

.PP
\fB--host\fP=""
	Exact mapped host/name; host labels may fall back to exporter instance

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Structured JSON, with missing values represented explicitly

.PP
\fB--netbox\fP=""
	Approved NetBox root URL (or LOCALHOST_NETBOX_URL)

.PP
\fB--prometheus\fP=""
	Approved Prometheus base URL (or LOCALHOST_PROMETHEUS_URL)

.PP
\fB--rack\fP=""
	Exact rack label/name

.PP
\fB--site\fP=""
	Exact site label/name

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Whole collection deadline (positive, at most 30s)


